{
  "$comment": "Cross-implementation conformance vectors for the C147 content-based package payload digest. atlas, mantle and design-system-Lifegames must all reproduce every expected digest byte for byte. A digest-spec change bumps specVersion and must update all three in one PR.",
  "specVersion": 1,
  "digest": "sha256 over the sorted, newline-joined \"<posix path> <sha256(normalized bytes)>\" lines. normalize: package.json is recursively key-sorted (arrays keep order) with the top-level version deleted; every other file is raw bytes. effectiveDigest additionally excludes any *.map whose sources[], resolved relative to the map's own directory, all land outside the packed file set.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "manifest-only",
      "why": "the minimum payload: package.json alone.",
      "files": {
        "package.json": "eyJuYW1lIjoiQHRveS94IiwidmVyc2lvbiI6IjEuMC4wIiwiZmlsZXMiOlsiZGlzdCJdfQ=="
      },
      "expectedStrictDigest": "a9d62524c927005004cd909e1a8b7a0341825e2f914339ffa895e2497230995b",
      "expectedEffectiveDigest": "a9d62524c927005004cd909e1a8b7a0341825e2f914339ffa895e2497230995b"
    },
    {
      "id": "manifest-key-order-a",
      "why": "key order A. Must produce the same digest as key-order-b — pnpm reinserts workspace dependency keys in resolution-completion order, so the same tree packs differently on consecutive runs.",
